    <section class="page-component-item">
      <div class="raw-html-content">
        <div class="raw-html-embed">
          <section class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec-h2">
            <div class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__container">
              <header class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__header">
                <h2 class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__h2" id="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec-h2">
                  What Formester accesses, what it does not
                </h2>
                <p class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__sub">
                  Drive integrations have a reputation for asking for too much. Formester does not.
                </p>
              </header>

              <ul class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__list">
                <li class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__item">
                  <span class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg
                      width="20"
                      height="20"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.8"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path>
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__h3">Scope requested: <code>drive.file</code></h3>
                    <p class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__body">
                      Formester sees and writes only files it created. It cannot read your existing Drive content,
                      search your Drive, or modify files it did not create.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__item">
                  <span class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg
                      width="20"
                      height="20"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.8"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <path
                        d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16z"
                      ></path>
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__h3">Storage owner</h3>
                    <p class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__body">
                      Files land in the Drive account that authorized the integration. The form respondent does not get
                      access to the destination folder.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__item">
                  <span class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg
                      width="20"
                      height="20"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.8"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-9-9c2.52 0 4.93 1 6.74 2.74L21 8"></path>
                      <path d="M21 3v5h-5"></path>
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__h3">Revoke anytime</h3>
                    <p class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__body">
                      Disconnect from Formester (<code>Integrations → Google Drive → Disconnect</code>) or revoke from
                      Google directly at
                      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. After
                      revoke, no new files write; existing files in your Drive stay untouched.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__item">
                  <span class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg
                      width="20"
                      height="20"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor"
                      stroke-width="1.8"
                      stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round"
                    >
                      <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2"></rect>
                      <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"></path>
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__h3">Encryption in transit</h3>
                    <p class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__body">TLS 1.2+ between Formester, Google's API, and your Drive.</p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__item" style="grid-column: 1 / -1">
                  <span class="fmstr-cmp-gdr-sec__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg
                      width="20"
                      height="20"
                      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                      fill="none"
